<%# locals: () %>
<%# The panel for assigning selected times to a billing. Visibility and selection
    are driven by the surrounding time-session-bulk controller, which lives in
    index.html.erb AROUND the turbo frame.

    Laid out after the design draft "Tickets Entschlackt" (user, 31.08.2026):
    a title with the count and the sum under it as a quiet subtitle, two plain
    radio choices whose field appears indented underneath the chosen one, a rule,
    and then the list of exactly what is about to be taken over. No boxes around
    the options: the panel is 420px wide and a card inside a card reads as two
    frames rather than one choice.

    From lg up it is a LANE beside the list, not a layer over it: as an overlay
    it covered the filters and the right-hand columns of the very rows the reader
    had just ticked. lg and not md: the lane is 420px, and on a 768px screen that
    leaves the list about 300px, where the titles truncate to nothing. Below it
    the panel is a sheet at the bottom edge, because there is no width to give.

    Which classes mean "closed" is declared ONCE, through the Stimulus classes
    API on the controller element. They appear in `class` below as well, because
    the panel has to render closed before any JavaScript runs or it would flash
    across the page on load. That the two agree is checked, not hoped for: see
    "the assignment panel" in spec/requests/organisations/time_sessions_table_spec.rb. %>
<%# z-mobile-nav, not z-modal: the phone's bottom navigation sits at 80 and
    floats exactly over the stacked Abbrechen/Zuweisen buttons, so at 50 the
    sheet's own actions were behind it.
    And a max height on the BASE, not only from md up: without one the sheet
    grows past the top of the screen and takes the title and the closing cross
    with it. dvh, because a phone's viewport changes height while the address bar
    comes and goes.

    The panel is a bounded COLUMN, and the scrolling happens one level in. It used
    to be a scroll box with three independently capped lists inside
    (30vh + 40vh + 20vh), and nothing budgeted for the header, the summaries, the
    total and the buttons on top of that. Every list kept to its cap and the
    panel still overflowed: measured at 760px viewport, "Zuweisen" left the
    visible area at the ELEVENTH selected booking, with 75px of the panel below
    the edge (user, 31.08.2026). Now the header and the buttons are fixed ends and
    what is between them scrolls, so the button cannot be pushed anywhere. %>
<div id="bulk-action-bar"
     class="fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-mobile-nav flex max-h-[85dvh] transform flex-col bg-cream-100 transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out
            border-t border-ink shadow-[0_-4px_0_0_#14110c]
            lg:sticky lg:inset-auto lg:top-4 lg:z-auto lg:w-[420px] lg:shrink-0
            lg:max-h-[calc(100vh-2rem)] lg:transform-none lg:self-start
            lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:shadow-none
            translate-y-full lg:hidden"
     data-time-session-bulk-target="actionBar"
     data-time-session-bulk-url="<%= bulk_assign_group_organisation_time_sessions_path(current_organisation) %>">
  <div class="flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col p-4 lg:p-6">
      <%# Title only. A count belongs here once at most, and the list below says
          it in the sentence that also says what happens to those rows: "Diese 5
          Zeiten werden übernommen", with the already-filed ones counted apart.
          A second count up here could only repeat that or contradict it, and it
          did contradict it: it named the whole selection (user, 31.08.2026). %>
      <%# The hairline is what makes the clipped row underneath read as scrolled
          content rather than as a rendering fault. A fixed header over a moving
          body needs an edge. %>
      <div class="mb-4 flex shrink-0 items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-cream-300 pb-3">
        <h3 class="min-w-0 text-lg font-bold leading-tight text-cream-900"
            tabindex="-1"
            data-time-session-bulk-target="panelTitle">
          <%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.panel_title') %>
        </h3>
        <div class="flex shrink-0 gap-2">
          <button type="button"
                  data-time-session-bulk-target="minimizeButton"
                  data-action="click->time-session-bulk#toggleMinimize"
                  <%# Only on the phone: a lane does not cover the list it
                      belongs to, so there is nothing to get out of the way of. %>
                  class="rounded p-2 text-cream-600 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-200 lg:hidden"
                  title="<%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.minimize_tooltip') %>">
            <i class="bi bi-chevron-down text-xl"></i>
          </button>
          <button type="button"
                  data-time-session-bulk-target="maximizeButton"
                  data-action="click->time-session-bulk#toggleMinimize"
                  class="hidden rounded p-2 text-cream-600 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-200 lg:hidden"
                  title="<%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.maximize_tooltip') %>">
            <i class="bi bi-chevron-up text-xl"></i>
          </button>
          <%# A bare cross, the way every other panel and modal in this app closes
              (see _cockpit_settings_modal): a plain button
              with a plain glyph, no Neo button component. It was a red danger
              button here, which reads as "delete something", and closing a panel
              destroys nothing. %>
          <button type="button"
                  class="p-1 text-cream-500 transition-colors hover:text-cream-700"
                  data-action="click->time-session-bulk#cancelBulkAssignment"
                  aria-label="<%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.close_tooltip') %>"
                  title="<%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.close_tooltip') %>">
            <i class="bi bi-x-lg" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Form Content (collapsible) -->
      <div class="flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col" data-time-session-bulk-target="formContent">
        <%# Everything between the two fixed ends. ONE scrollbar: the lists inside
            no longer carry caps of their own, because a cap is an attempt to
            solve by arithmetic what the column solves by structure. The billings
            keep theirs, see there. %>
        <div class="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto">
        <%# ONE list, not a choice of kind followed by a choice of thing. The
            kind was implied by the answer all along: pick a billing and you have
            said "an existing one", type a name and you have said "a new one", so
            asking first made the reader supply the same fact twice. It also cost
            the common case a click AND hid it: "eine neue Abrechnung" was the
            preselected option, so the panel opened showing no billings at all
            (user, 31.08.2026).

            The new-billing row is a member of the same radio group. It carries
            the same box, so the list has one control and one meaning: this is
            where the time goes. %>
          <div>
            <% if unbilled_time_session_groups.any? %>
              <%# The one list that keeps a cap. Not to protect the buttons, which
                  the column does now, but so that a long list of billings does
                  not have to be scrolled past to reach what is being assigned:
                  this is the input, the lists below are the evidence. At five
                  billings it measures 156px against a 228px cap and never
                  engages. %>
              <ul class="max-h-[30vh] space-y-1 overflow-y-auto">
                <% unbilled_time_session_groups.each do |group| %>
                  <li>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
                    <%# The radio itself is sr-only, so the ROW has to show the focus. Without
                        this a keyboard reader moves through the billings with nothing
                        on screen telling them where they are. %>
                    <label class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded px-1 py-1.5 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-200 has-[:checked]:bg-cream-200 has-[:focus-visible]:ring-2 has-[:focus-visible]:ring-ink lg:py-1">
                      <%# data-minutes so the panel can say what this billing
                          BECOMES, without asking the server again. %>
                      <input type="radio"
                             name="existing_group_id"
                             value="<%= group.id %>"
                             class="peer sr-only"
                             data-minutes="<%= unbilled_time_session_group_minutes.fetch(group.id, 0) %>"
                             data-time-session-bulk-target="existingGroupOption"
                             data-action="click->time-session-bulk#togglePick change->time-session-bulk#chooseBilling">
                      <%# A VISIBLE box in front of every line, empty until one is
                          picked. It used to be a dot that appeared only once
                          something was chosen, so an untouched list showed no
                          control at all: the reader saw a name and never learnt
                          that a choice was still owed (user, 31.08.2026).

                          The input stays a RADIO, because only one billing can
                          take the time. The box is the affordance, not the
                          semantics: a lone radio circle reads as an ornament,
                          especially with one billing in the list, while a box
                          reads as something to tick. Screen readers hear the
                          radio group either way.

                          Two spans rather than one, because peer-checked matches
                          SIBLINGS of the input: a checkmark nested inside a
                          single box would never see the state. %>
                      <span aria-hidden="true"
                            class="flex h-[18px] w-[18px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded border-2 border-cream-400 bg-surface transition-colors peer-checked:hidden"></span>
                      <span aria-hidden="true"
                            class="hidden h-[18px] w-[18px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded border-2 border-ink bg-ink text-on-fill peer-checked:flex">
                        <i class="bi bi-check text-sm leading-none"></i>
                      </span>
                      <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate font-mono text-sm text-cream-700 peer-checked:font-bold peer-checked:text-cream-900">
                        <%= group.name %>
                      </span>
                      <%# What it holds today, and, once it is the chosen one,
                          what it becomes. Only on the chosen line: every line
                          showing its own hypothetical would be a column of
                          numbers of which at most one can ever happen, and it
                          would bury the totals you are comparing.
                          Time, not money: nothing in this app carries a rate, so
                          a currency here would be invented. %>
                      <span class="flex shrink-0 items-baseline gap-1 font-mono text-xs">
                        <span class="text-cream-600">
                          <%= TimeSession.format_duration(unbilled_time_session_group_minutes.fetch(group.id, 0)) %>
                        </span>
                        <span class="hidden font-bold text-cream-900" data-billing-result></span>
                      </span>
                    </label>
                    <%# A control of its OWN, not the row: the row already means
                        "assign to this one", and one element cannot mean both
                        "choose" and "let me look first". Same chevron the time
                        list rows use. %>
                    <button type="button"
                            class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded text-cream-500 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-200 hover:text-cream-900 lg:h-6 lg:w-6"
                            data-action="click->time-session-bulk#toggleBillingEntries"
                            aria-controls="billing_entries_<%= group.id %>"
                            aria-expanded="false"
                            title="<%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.billing_entries_toggle') %>"
                            aria-label="<%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.billing_entries_toggle') %>">
                      <i class="bi bi-chevron-right text-xs transition-transform duration-200" data-billing-chevron></i>
                    </button>
                    </div>

                    <%# loading="lazy" means Turbo fetches this the first time it
                        becomes VISIBLE, so unhiding the wrapper is the whole
                        loading mechanism: no fetch of ours, and nothing is
                        requested for a billing nobody opened. %>
                    <div class="hidden pl-2" data-billing-entries>
                      <turbo-frame id="billing_entries_<%= group.id %>"
                                   src="<%= entries_organisation_time_session_group_path(current_organisation, group) %>"
                                   loading="lazy">
                        <p class="py-1 text-xs italic leading-6 text-cream-500">
                          <%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.billing_entries_loading') %>
                        </p>
                      </turbo-frame>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                <% end %>
              </ul>
            <% else %>
              <p class="px-1 py-1.5 text-sm text-cream-600"><%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.existing_group_none') %></p>
            <% end %>

            <%# The escape hatch, PINNED under the scrolling list rather than the
                last row inside it. The list of billings scrolls, and a row at the
                bottom of a scrolling box is a row you have to find; this one has
                to be reachable at any number of billings. Same reason the sum
                hangs under the selection list further down, and the same shape.

                Under and not above: the billings are the likely answer, and a
                blank field on line one would push them out of first place.

                Sans, not the mono the billing names wear: those are identifiers
                that exist, this is a thing to do. %>
            <div class="mt-1 border-t border-cream-300 pt-1">
              <label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded px-1 py-1.5 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-200 has-[:checked]:bg-cream-200 has-[:focus-visible]:ring-2 has-[:focus-visible]:ring-ink lg:py-1">
                <%# Same radio group as the billings above, which is what makes
                    the whole thing one choice. The value is never read: the
                    controller knows this row by its TARGET, and the submit is
                    built by hand, so no sentinel string has to agree across two
                    languages. %>
                <input type="radio"
                       name="existing_group_id"
                       value="new"
                       class="peer sr-only"
                       data-time-session-bulk-target="newGroupOption"
                       data-action="click->time-session-bulk#togglePick change->time-session-bulk#chooseBilling">
                <span aria-hidden="true"
                      class="flex h-[18px] w-[18px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded border-2 border-cream-400 bg-surface transition-colors peer-checked:hidden"></span>
                <span aria-hidden="true"
                      class="hidden h-[18px] w-[18px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded border-2 border-ink bg-ink text-on-fill peer-checked:flex">
                  <i class="bi bi-check text-sm leading-none"></i>
                </span>
                <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-sm text-cream-700 peer-checked:font-bold peer-checked:text-cream-900">
                  <%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.new_group_option') %>
                </span>
              </label>

              <%# Indented under its own row and only while that row is picked.
                  Disabled as well as hidden: a hidden but enabled field still
                  submits, and validateForm reads the value. %>
              <div class="hidden pl-7 pt-1" data-time-session-bulk-target="newGroupField">
                <input type="text"
                       autocomplete="off"
                       disabled
                       placeholder="<%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.new_group_placeholder') %>"
                       class="w-full rounded-lg border border-cream-300 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-sm focus:border-ink focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-ink"
                       data-time-session-bulk-target="newGroupName"
                       data-action="input->time-session-bulk#validateForm">
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        <%# What will actually be taken over, one line each, droppable.
            The rows of the list are folded by default, so ticking a row picks
            bookings the reader cannot see; this is where they become visible.
            Rendered by the controller from its selection rather than server-side,
            because it has to follow every click AND has to keep naming a booking
            that a filter has since taken off the screen. %>
        <%# A booking can already be in the billing it is being assigned to: the
            list lets you pick one out of billing X and hand it to billing X
            again. It is not an error and there is nothing to forbid, but it is
            not a transfer either, and counting its minutes into the result would
            add time the billing already holds. So it is listed apart, under its
            own heading, and left out of the arithmetic (user, 31.08.2026). %>
        <div class="mb-4 mt-5 hidden border-t border-cream-300 pt-4" data-time-session-bulk-target="selectionPanel">
          <%# Heading, list and total appear and disappear together, so they hang
              on ONE wrapper rather than each carrying the same condition. Its
              twin is alreadyPanel below, which already had this shape. %>
          <div data-time-session-bulk-target="takenPanel">
            <p class="mb-2 text-xs text-cream-600" data-time-session-bulk-target="selectionSummary"></p>
            <%# No cap. This is the block that grows with the reader's work, and
                it used to carry one so it could not push "Zuweisen" off the
                panel. It pushed it off anyway at eleven selections, because the
                cap only bounded this list and nothing bounded the sum of the
                parts. The buttons are a fixed end of the column now, so there is
                nothing left for a cap here to protect. %>
            <ul class="space-y-0.5" data-time-session-bulk-target="selectionList"></ul>

            <%# The total of what is about to be taken over, in the same 46px slot
                the single durations use, so it stands under the column it adds up.
                OUTSIDE the scrolling list on purpose: inside it, the one number
                the reader came for would scroll away with the rows.
                It counts this list and nothing else. The bookings under it are
                already in the billing and bring no minutes, which is why they are
                listed apart in the first place. %>
            <div class="mt-1 flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-cream-300 pt-1 text-xs leading-6">
              <span class="w-[46px] shrink-0 font-mono font-bold text-cream-900"
                    data-time-session-bulk-target="selectionTotal">00:00</span>
              <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-cream-600">
                <%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.selection_total') %>
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="hidden" data-time-session-bulk-target="alreadyPanel">
            <p class="mb-2 mt-4 text-xs text-cream-600" data-time-session-bulk-target="alreadySummary"></p>
            <ul class="space-y-0.5" data-time-session-bulk-target="alreadyList"></ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        </div>
        <%# The other fixed end. mt-4 rather than the old block margins: the
            scroll region above ends where it ends. %>
        <div class="mt-4 flex shrink-0 flex-col justify-end gap-2 sm:flex-row">
          <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
            variant: :secondary,
            size: :medium,
            data: { action: "click->time-session-bulk#cancelBulkAssignment" }
          ) do %>
            <%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.cancel_button') %>
          <% end %>

          <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
            variant: :primary,
            size: :medium,
            disabled: true,
            data: {
              time_session_bulk_target: "submitButton",
              action: "click->time-session-bulk#submitBulkAssignment"
            }
          ) do %>
            <%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.assign_button') %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- End of formContent -->
  </div>
</div>
